{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,22]],"date-time":"2026-09-22T20:19:58Z","timestamp":1790108398389,"version":"4.0.1"},"reference-count":57,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"7","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2024,10,23]],"date-time":"2024-10-23T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1729641600000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":22,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/100004421","name":"World Bank Group","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100004421","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Energy Storage"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,10]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>ABSTRACT<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    Biomass and biowaste resources can be used to create self\u2010doped carbon with a distinctive microstructure. Using an economical and environmentally friendly method to create heteroatom\u2010doped carbon electrode materials with excellent electrochemical performance has attracted much attention in the energy storage industry. A novel facile two\u2010step, low\u2010cost, and eco\u2010friendly synthesis method for\n                    <jats:italic>Colocasia esculenta<\/jats:italic>\n                    peels has been developed to manufacture activated carbon (CEPAC) and used as an electrode material for supercapacitor application. The CEPAC 1:1 displayed a high specific surface area of 910\u2009m\n                    <jats:sup>2<\/jats:sup>\n                    \/g with oxygen\u2010heteroatom polar sites in the carbon network. A specific capacitance of 525.3\u2009F\/g was recorded in the three\u2010electrode system using a 3\u2009M KOH solution. The assembled symmetric cell delivered an impressive specific capacitance of 98.7\u2009F\/g at 1\u2009A\/g while maintaining 98.4% of the initially recorded capacitance after 10\u2009000 charge\u2013discharge cycles. These results present a promising low\u2010cost and simple processing route for synthesizing electrode materials with superior surface properties for high\u2010performance supercapacitors.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/est2.70057","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,10,23]],"date-time":"2024-10-23T06:49:39Z","timestamp":1729666179000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":10,"title":["Facile Synthesis of\n                    <i>Colocasia esculenta<\/i>\n                    Peels\u2010Derived Activated Carbon for High\u2010Performance Supercapacitor"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"6","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0007-9073-7194","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Daniel\u00a0Nframah","family":"Ampong","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Materials Engineering, College of Engineering Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Technology  Kumasi Ghana"},{"name":"National Institute for Materials Advancement Pittsburg State University  Pittsburg Kansas USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Perseverance","family":"Dzikunu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Materials Engineering, College of Engineering Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Technology  Kumasi Ghana"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Frank\u00a0Ofori","family":"Agyemang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Materials Engineering, College of Engineering Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Technology  Kumasi Ghana"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Patrick","family":"Aggrey","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Center for Energy Science and Technology Skolkovo Institute of Science and Technology  Moscow Russia"}],"role":[{"vocab